WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.679 --> 00:00:04.824
Eh, try this. Your shop got a stock list: tea, rice.

2
00:00:04.844 --> 00:00:07.864
You scared later you spoil it, so you make a backup:

3
00:00:07.884 --> 00:00:12.224
backup equals stock. Then you append oats to the backup only.

4
00:00:12.244 --> 00:00:13.427
Now print stock.

5
00:00:14.227 --> 00:00:16.664
Walao eh, oats inside stock also!

6
00:00:16.684 --> 00:00:18.744
Your backup go and change the original.

7
00:00:18.764 --> 00:00:19.574
How come?

8
00:00:19.804 --> 00:00:21.304
Today 3 things lah.

9
00:00:21.324 --> 00:00:25.984
Aliasing versus copying. Functions that CHANGE your list versus functions that

10
00:00:26.004 --> 00:00:27.224
return a new one.

11
00:00:27.244 --> 00:00:30.544
And nested lists, list inside list.

12
00:00:30.564 --> 00:00:34.054
After this, this kind of question cannot bluff you already.

13
00:00:36.065 --> 00:00:39.485
Step 1: stock equals tea, rice.

14
00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:42.915
Python make 1 list and stick the name stock on it.

15
00:00:42.945 --> 00:00:45.645
Step 2: backup equals stock.

16
00:00:45.665 --> 00:00:46.835
Got new list or not?

17
00:00:47.315 --> 00:00:50.765
Don't have! Python only stick a second NAME on the same

18
00:00:50.785 --> 00:00:54.125
list. Like 1 kopi cup with 2 name stickers.

19
00:00:54.145 --> 00:00:57.445
Step 3: backup dot append oats.

20
00:00:57.465 --> 00:01:01.405
The cup change, so both names see tea, rice, oats.

21
00:01:01.425 --> 00:01:03.409
This one we call aliasing.

22
00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:07.329
Why ah? Because a list is mutable, can change after you

23
00:01:07.349 --> 00:01:10.809
make it, and the equals sign NEVER copy a list.

24
00:01:10.829 --> 00:01:14.369
You want a real copy, write spare equals stock with a

25
00:01:14.389 --> 00:01:17.809
full slice, just a colon inside the square brackets.

26
00:01:17.829 --> 00:01:19.409
Or list of stock.

27
00:01:19.429 --> 00:01:20.779
Now got 2 cups.

28
00:01:20.949 --> 00:01:25.679
So the trap: backup equals stock is NOT a backup lah.

29
00:01:27.743 --> 00:01:31.723
Now functions. You pass a list into a function, the function

30
00:01:31.743 --> 00:01:33.073
get a copy or not?

31
00:01:33.107 --> 00:01:36.607
No copy! The parameter is just 1 more name for YOUR

32
00:01:36.627 --> 00:01:40.127
list. Look at restock, with counts and amount.

33
00:01:40.147 --> 00:01:43.687
Inside: counts at i, plus equals amount.

34
00:01:43.707 --> 00:01:47.807
That one change the caller's list directly, and it return None.

35
00:01:47.827 --> 00:01:49.927
Then restocked, with a d.

36
00:01:49.947 --> 00:01:54.527
It start with result equals empty list, append count plus amount,

37
00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:57.677
return result. Your old list stay the same.

38
00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.567
How to know which is which ah?

39
00:01:59.587 --> 00:02:03.487
Read the ARROW. Arrow None: it change your list.

40
00:02:03.507 --> 00:02:06.527
Arrow list: it give you a new one, so you must

41
00:02:06.547 --> 00:02:07.197
store it.

42
00:02:07.948 --> 00:02:11.918
The trap: you call restocked but never store the answer.

43
00:02:12.068 --> 00:02:14.718
Then nothing happen, wasted lor.

44
00:02:16.732 --> 00:02:19.102
Next, list inside list.

45
00:02:19.132 --> 00:02:24.112
shelves got 2 inner lists: 4, 0, 6 and 2, 5,

46
00:02:24.132 --> 00:02:26.712
1. Each one is 1 shelf.

47
00:02:26.732 --> 00:02:29.632
Now shelves at 1, then at 0.

48
00:02:29.652 --> 00:02:34.112
Read from the left: FIRST pick shelf 1, then item 0.

49
00:02:34.132 --> 00:02:37.752
Answer is 2. len of shelves is 2, that is the

50
00:02:37.772 --> 00:02:41.592
shelves. len of shelves at 0 is 3, the items on

51
00:02:41.612 --> 00:02:42.582
that shelf.

52
00:02:42.718 --> 00:02:45.032
And the names game still on hor.

53
00:02:45.052 --> 00:02:48.552
Copy shelves with a full slice, you only copy the OUTER

54
00:02:48.572 --> 00:02:51.312
list. The inner shelves still shared.

55
00:02:51.332 --> 00:02:54.045
Change 1 inner item, both sides see it.

56
00:02:54.065 --> 00:02:55.462
Dun play play.

57
00:02:57.679 --> 00:03:01.830
So the one-line takeaway: the equals sign give a new NAME,

58
00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:03.430
never a new list.

59
00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:05.350
Want a copy, slice it.

60
00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:08.150
Want to know if a function change your list, read the

61
00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:08.940
arrow.

62
00:03:08.974 --> 00:03:13.234
The practice notebook got 6 exercises in the same small shop.

63
00:03:13.254 --> 00:03:16.554
3 to predict, 1 fix the bug, and 2 you write

64
00:03:16.574 --> 00:03:19.834
from scratch: fill up a shelf in place, and totals per

65
00:03:19.854 --> 00:03:21.584
shelf with 2 loops.

66
00:03:21.618 --> 00:03:25.438
Last thing: graded work must be your OWN, the course does

67
00:03:25.458 --> 00:03:27.118
not allow AI on it.

68
00:03:27.138 --> 00:03:30.691
Practise here until steady, then that one you do yourself.

69
00:03:30.711 --> 00:03:31.628
Jia you!
